investing 14% of profits supports about 2.2% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.5% a year over five years.","Capex runs 1.6x depreciation (15.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 24, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 63.0% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own 9.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 89%.","It returns 4.0% a year to shareholders (1.6% in buybacks and 2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 3.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 14.1% of the float, 3.7 days to cover."],"people":["With about 9,500 employees, each generates about $212K of revenue, 0.6x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 3.7% a year.","That works out to $31K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.6M (17x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":65,"head":"Invest: trades 43% below fair value of $84.55; ROIC 15.3% vs WACC 8.2%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 54, gates 13/24)","Trades 43% below fair value of $84.55","ROIC 15.3% vs WACC 8.2%","FCF margin 14.4%","Revenue grew 11.2%/yr over 5y"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 4.1x","Interest coverage only 3.0x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.78)","P/E 24.4x vs sector 19.3x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":71.87,"vc":{"base":84.55,"base_src":"dcf","bear":54.0,"bull":130.69,"alt_median":22.77,"n_alt":3,"gap":3.4401,"dispersion":0.2452,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 344% above the other models' median ($22.77)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"RRR","date":"2026-11-06"}